of injuries in Ethiopia from 1990-2017: evidence from the global burden of disease study. Inj Epidemiol. 2020. [cited 2020 December 21];7:67. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] [71]. Misganaw A, HMariam D, Araya T. Association of socioeconomic and behavioral factors with adult mortality: analysis of data from verbal autopsy in Addis Ababa, Ethiopia. BMC Public Health. 2013;13:1–12. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] [72]. Byass P, Berhane Y, Emmelin A, et al. The role of Demographic Surveillance Systems (DSS) in assessing the health of communities: an example from rural Ethiopia. Public Health. 2002;116:145–150. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] [73]. Ae-Ngibise K, Masanja H, Kellerman R, et al. Risk factors for injury mortality in rural Tanzania: a secondary data analysis. BMJ Open. 2012;2:e001721. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] [74]. Adebowale O, Julia V. External causes of death, National end of life care intelligence network. 2011. cited 2021 Oct 10]. Available from 2021 Oct 10: https://www.bl.uk/britishlibrary/~/media/bl/global/social-welfare/pdfs/non-secure/e/x/t/external-causes-of-death.pdf . [75]. Mberu B, Wamukoya M, Oti S, et al. Trends in causes of adult deaths among the Urban poor: evidence from Nairobi urban health and demographic surveillance system, 2003-2012. J Urban Health Bull N Y Acad Med. 2015;92:422–445. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] [76]. Population-Reference-Bureau . Noncommunicable diseases among older adults in low- and middle-income countries. 2012. cited 2021 Oct 12]. Available from 2021 Oct 12: https://www.prb.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/TRA26-2012-NCD-aging.pdf . [77]. Schneider E. Infectious diseases in the elderly. Ann Intern Med. 1983;98:395–400. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] [78]. Fleischer N Social patterning of chronic disease risk factors: Cross-national and within-country comparisons[dissertation]. [Michigan: ]: