[ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 47. Chaurasiya D, Gupta A, Chauhan S, Patel R, Chaurasia V. Age, period and birth cohort effects on prevalence of obesity among reproductive-age women in India. SSM Popul Health. 2019;9. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] 48. Mohan V, Mathur P, Deepa R, Deepa M, Shukla DK, Menon GR, et al. Urban rural differences in prevalence of self-reported diabetes in India—The WHO–ICMR Indian NCD risk factor surveillance. Diabetes Res Clin Pract. 2008;80:159–168. doi: 10.1016/j.diabres.2007.11.018. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 49. Cantarero-Prieto D, Pascual-Sáez M, Blázquez-Fernández C. Social isolation and multiple chronic diseases after age 50: A European macro-regional analysis. PLoS ONE. 2018;13:e0205062. doi: 10.1371/journal.pone.0205062. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Associated Data This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article. Supplementary Materials Additional file 1: (25.6KB, docx) Additional file 2: (20.4KB, docx) Data Availability Statement The datasets generated and/or analysed during the current study are available with the International Institute for Population Sciences, Mumbai, India repository and could be accessed from the following link: https://iipsindia.ac.in/sites/default/files/LASI_DataRequestForm_0.pdf . Those who wish to download the data have to follow the above link. This link leads to a data request form designed by International Institute for Population Sciences. After completing the form, it should be mailed to: datacenter@iips.net for further processing. After successfully sending the mail, individual will receive the data in a reasonable time.',20,'2025-10-10 07:02:17','2025-10-10 07:02:17');
