y/exercise and type 2 diabetes: a consensus statement from the American Diabetes Association. Diabetes care. 2006;29(6):1433–8.[DOI: 10.2337/dc06-9910]. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] 52. D’Agostino RB, Hamman RF, Karter AJ, Mykkanen L, Wagenknecht LE, Haffner SM. Cardiovascular disease risk factors predict the development of type 2 diabetes: the insulin resistance atherosclerosis study. Diabetes care. 2004;27(9):2234–40.[DOI: 10.2337/diacare.27.9.]. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] 53. Maddah M. Association of diabetes with living area in Iranian women. International journal of cardiology. 2010;143(1):100–2.[DOI: 10.1016/j.ijcard.2008.11.171]. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] 54. Bachmann M, Eachus J, Hopper C, Davey Smith G, Propper C, Pearson N, et al. Socio-economic inequalities in diabetes complications, control, attitudes and health service use: a cross-sectional study. Diabetic Medicine. 2003;20(11):921–9.[DOI: 10.1046/j.464-5491.2003.01050.x]. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] 55. Peykari N, Djalalinia S, Qorbani M, Sobhani S, Farzadfar F, Larijani B. Socioeconomic inequalities and diabetes: A systematic review from Iran. Journal of Diabetes & Metabolic Disorders. 2015;14(1):8.[DOI: 10.1186/s40200-015-0135-4]. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] 56. Burrows S, Auger N, Gamache P, Hamel D. Individual and area socioeconomic inequalities in cause-specific unintentional injury mortality: 11-year follow-up study of 2.7 million Canadians. Accident Analysis & Prevention. 2012;45:99–106.[DOI: 10.1016/j.aap.2011.11.010]. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] 57. Cho H-J, Khang Y-H, Yang S, Harper S, Lynch JW. Socioeconomic differentials in cause-specific mortality among South Korean adolescents. International journal of epidemiology. 2007;36(1):50–7.[DOI: 10.1093/ije/dyl239]. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] 58. Phelan JC, Link BG, Tehranifar P. Social conditions as fundamental causes of health inequalities: theory, evidence, and policy implications. Journal of health and social behavior. 2010;51(1_suppl):S28-S40.[DOI: 10.1177/0022146510383498]. [ D