w of the good, the bad and the ugly. N Z Med J. 2003;116:U465. [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Canadian Nurses Association Code of Ethics for Registered Nurses. http://cna-aiic.ca/cna/documents/pdf/publications/CodeofEthics2002_e.pdf Canadian Medical Association . CMA Code of Ethics. Ottawa; 2004. [ Google Scholar ] American Medical Association Physician obligation in disaster preparedness and response. http://www.ama-assn.org/apps/pf_new/pf_online?f_n=browse&doc=policyfiles/HnE/E-9.067.HTM [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] Canadian Medical Association . CMA Code of Ethics. Ottawa; 1922. [ Google Scholar ] Huber S, Wynia M. When pestilence prevails. Physician responsibilities in epidemics. Am J Bioeth. 2004;4:5–11. doi: 10.1162/152651604773067497. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Emanuel EJ. The lessons of SARS. Ann Intern Med. 2003;139:589–591. doi: 10.7326/0003-4819-139-7-200310070-00011. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Ontario Medical Association Protecting the rights and safety of physicians and families in the event of public emergency. http://www.oma.org/pcomm/omr/feb/06bill56.htm Mills EJ, Singh S, Singh JA, Orbinski JJ, Warren M, Upshur RE. Designing research in vulnerable populations: lessons from HIV prevention trials that stopped early. BMJ. 2005;331:1403–1406. doi: 10.1136/bmj.331.7529.1403. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] University of Toronto Joint Centre for Bioethics . Stand on guard for thee: Ethical considerations in preparedness planning for pandemic influenza. a report of the University of Toronto Joint Centre for Bioethics Panedemic Influenza Working Group; http://www.utoronto.ca/jcb/home/documents/pandemic.pdf [ Google Scholar ]',26,'2025-10-10 07:04:01','2025-10-10 07:04:01');
